<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- DEVICE (sideload) entitlements: deliberately EMPTY.

     Nothing here is an oversight — each entitlement was removed for a reason, and an empty set is
     exactly what a free Apple ID personal team can sign without friction:

       - com.apple.security.application-groups: team-scoped, not issued to free personal teams. The
         GainsWidget target that needed it is gone.
       - com.apple.developer.healthkit: also unavailable on a free team (Gains never appeared under
         iOS Settings → Health → Data Access & Devices). Weight now comes from Whoop, and the whole
         Apple Health integration has been removed rather than left as a dead button.
       - keychain-access-groups: KeychainStore passes a nil access group on device (see the
         #if targetEnvironment(simulator) split), so iOS grants the app's automatic default group.
         Declaring one would only risk a signing mismatch. Whoop tokens persist normally. -->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
</dict>
</plist>
